    "result": "Perfect! The fix is built and working. I can see in the compiled output (lines 635-639) that the `--ci` flag is being properly passed through to frai-gate.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. Here's what was happening and how I fixed it:\n\n### The Problem\nThe `--ci` flag was being consumed by the main program's option parser (defined on line 605) before the `gate` subcommand could access it. When you ran `frai gate init --ci`, the flag wasn't included in the arguments passed to frai-gate.\n\n### The Solution\nModified `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d07/with/t1-flag-bug/r2/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to check if `--ci` is present in `process.argv` and explicitly pass it through to frai-gate when spawning the subprocess.\n\n### Verification\n\u2713 **With `--ci`**: `frai gate init --ci` now creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`  \n\u2713 **Without `--ci`**: `frai gate init` still creates only `FRAI-SPEC.md` (no workflow directory)\n\nThe package has been rebuilt and is ready to use. You can commit the changes with:\n```bash\ngit add packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js\ngit commit -m \"Fix: frai gate init --ci now creates GitHub Actions workflow\"\n```",
